  "details": "<p><a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1348/\">Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>\u00a0in 2011 as part of the \"Ancient Villages of Northern Syria\" under criteria iii, iv, and v of UNESCO's World Heritage List\u00a0<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://whc.unesco.org/en/criteria/\">Operational Guidelines</a>.</p>\r\n<p>Specific archaeological components include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A <strong>praetorium</strong> of the Roman headquarters</li>\r\n<li>A <strong>temple</strong> and <strong>grottoes</strong> for pagan worship</li>\r\n<li>A <strong>Byzantine basilica</strong></li>\r\n<li>A large communal <strong>reservoir</strong></li>\r\n<li>The surroundings contain vestiges of the <strong>Roman road</strong> that led to Antioch</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ul>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient place, located in modern Syria, with remains of Roman praetorium, a temple and grottoes for pagan worship, a Byzantine basilica, and a large communal reservoir. Inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2011 as part of the \"Ancient Villages of Northern Syria.\"",
